{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"be549cf605f93aa3164b0550875d0abd189c78f307e1264cbe21970dbdb6cf4e","digest":{"component_or_area":"complexity baseline gate (scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py)","key_entities":["scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py","lock_against_base","_fetch_base_ceilings_from_main","_base_commit_for_comparison",".github/complexity-baseline.json","src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","close_ticket","tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py"],"problem_keywords":["complexity gate","baseline comparison","merge base","ceiling reduction","un-rebased branches","CI lock"],"propositions":["The complexity lock compares branch ceilings against main tip instead of merge-base, causing un-rebased branches to fail when main lowers a ceiling","Every open change carrying a pre-reduction baseline presents the old ceiling value against main's new lower value, which the lock incorrectly interprets as a ceiling raise by the branch","The _fetch_base_ceilings_from_main fetch uses --depth=1 which is too shallow to compute a merge base between main and the branch","The fix must compare branch baseline against merge-base(main, HEAD) and fall back to main-tip comparison only when merge base cannot be computed, preserving fail-closed semantics","A branch that genuinely raises a ceiling or adds a new entry relative to its fork point must still fail the lock after the fix"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787639327503469001,"uuid":"d613513e-4446-46a9-9bb6-c9d823a31ef5"}